          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joel 1:2",
        "book": "Joel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Tell ye your children of it, and let your children tell their children, and their children another generation.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joel 1:3",
        "book": "Joel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "That which the palmerworm hath left hath the locust eaten; and that which the locust hath left hath the cankerworm eaten; and that which the cankerworm hath left hath the caterpiller eaten.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "IE The invading or conquering armies are compared to four varieties (or stages of growth) of locusts."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Lev. 26:24 (14–38)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joel 1:4",
        "book": "Joel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Awake, ye drunkards, and weep; and howl, all ye drinkers of wine, because of the new wine; for it is cut off from your mouth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "Isa. 32:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
