        "reference": "Joel 1:6",
        "book": "Joel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath laid my vine waste, and barked my fig tree: he hath made it clean bare, and cast it away; the branches thereof are made white.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 91
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joel 1:7",
        "book": "Joel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Lament like a virgin girded with sackcloth for the husband of her youth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Ezek. 16:32 (32–38)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joel 1:8",
        "book": "Joel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "The meat offering and the drink offering is cut off from the house of the Lord; the priests, the Lord’s ministers, mourn.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joel 1:9",
        "book": "Joel",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "The field is wasted, the land mourneth; for the corn is wasted: the new wine is dried up, the oil languisheth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Hosea 4:3; D&C 43:25 (24–25); 87:6 (1–8); JS—M 1:29."
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "OR grain."
